{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/122317","id":4256670403,"node_id":"PR_kwDOAO6SJc79t6LD","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/122317","diff_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/122317.diff","patch_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/122317.patch","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/122317","commits_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/122317/commits","review_comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/122317/comments","review_comment_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/comments{/number}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/122317/comments","statuses_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/statuses/5913cd27514fab93a4bdfb04167e46f36562ea96","number":122317,"state":"closed","locked":false,"title":"Fail when attempting to profile in release exports","user":{"login":"HolonProduction","id":99511741,"node_id":"U_kgDOBe5tvQ","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/99511741?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/HolonProduction","html_url":"https://github.com/HolonProduction","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/HolonProduction/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/HolonProduction/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/HolonProduction/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/HolonProduction/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/HolonProduction/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/HolonProduction/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/HolonProduction/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/HolonProduction/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/HolonProduction/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"## What problem(s) does this PR solve?\r\n\r\n- Spiritual successor to https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/122213\r\n- While working on https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/122210 I got into profiler territory. A lot of this stuff is provably useless in release builds. So we should restrict access to it early as well.\r\n\r\n## Additional information\r\n\r\n- I decided to adopt `ifdef DEBUG_ENABLED` over `defined(DEBUG_ENABLED) || defined(TOOLS_ENABLED)` since tools imply debugging at the moment. And looking at the internals I don't see that changing.\r\n- The main loop changes are not compat breaking, we print an error if users pass `--profiling` but continue. The `ifdef` condition can provably never happen, since `EngineDebugger::is_active` can't be true in release builds.\r\n- This PR includes a second change, which makes `EngineDebugger::profiler_add_frame_data` a no-op if the specified profiler is not actively profiling.\r\n  - Activating a profiler in release builds impossible: https://github.com/HolonProduction/godot/blob/5913cd27514fab93a4bdfb04167e46f36562ea96/core/core_bind.cpp#L2213 (the guard is only in core bind, but the internal version is not called in release builds).\r\n  - However the registration infrastructure for profilers is functional in release builds.\r\n  - Since `profiler_add_frame_data` was not guarded against inactive profilers, one could theoretically abuse this infrastructure as a message broker in release builds. This is obviously not a valid usecase and fine to forbid. However I felt this detail would have gotten lost in https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/122210 which focuses on verifiably safe exclusions.","labels":[{"id":73330066,"node_id":"MDU6TGFiZWw3MzMzMDA2Ng==","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/labels/enhancement","name":"enhancement","description":"","color":"aaccff","default":true,"archived_at":null,"archived_by":null},{"id":279097966,"node_id":"MDU6TGFiZWwyNzkwOTc5NjY=","url":"https://api.g